\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : U.S. Dollar Gains As Japan Halts Yen's Rise\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 06:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 By Myra P. Saefong\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar climbed against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia's Wednesday afternoon trading after Japan took action in the global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in a bid to halt the yen's advance against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index (DXY), which tracks the performance of the greenback against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traded at 81.691, down from 81.064 late North American trading Tuesday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda confirmed that his ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets but didn't specify the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , according to reports.\par \par \uc2 "The move follows weeks of verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese authorities," said Mitul Kotecha, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Credit Agricole.\par \par \uc2 The action also came a day after a leadership election for the ruling Democratic Party of Japan, in which Prime Minister Naoto Kan survived an internal challenge to his leadership.\par \par \uc2 By Wednesday afternoon in Asia, one U.S. dollar bought \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A584.90, rebounding from a more than 15-year low of \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A582.85 seen before the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar traded at 83.13 late Tuesday in North America.\par \par \uc2 Japan joins the club\par \par \uc2 "When viewed from the perspective of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has put \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in line with other Asian central banks, which have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Kotecha.\par \par \uc2 "However, Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has merely slowed the appreciation in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to be satisfied with a similar result," he said.\par \par \uc2 Also, the "sensitivity of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general to the [dollar-yen rate] has lessened considerably over recent months, but still remains significant for some such as" the Malaysian ringgit, Singapore dollar, Philippine peso and Thai baht, said Kotecha.\par \par \uc2 Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates show that the U.S. dollar at 3.1185 ringgit from 3.1040 ringgit late in North American trading Tuesday; at 1.3376 Singapore dollars versus S$1.3328; at 44.372 pesos versus 44.030 pesos; and at 30.83 baht vs 30.74 baht, according to Thomson Reuters data reported by Dow Jones Newswires.\par \par \uc2 Against the U.S. dollar, the euro bought $1.2961, down from $1.3024 late Tuesday in North American trading.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 15, 2010 00:20 ET (04:20 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100915e69f000se\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
