\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ BEAT WATCH: Japanese Equities May Reap  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Benefit\b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Nurse  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 12:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2010, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted to try and stem the recent rise in the yen Wednesday, instructing the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. And equities could reap the rewards of this move.\par \par \uc2 The action by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , its first \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six and a half years, followed the yen hitting a fresh 15-year high against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Dealers said the Japanese authorities repeatedly bought the dollar against the yen, starting in morning trade in Tokyo. That resulted in the greenback hitting a high of Y85.54, up from the fresh 15-year low at Y82.87 the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had marked shortly before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began.\par \par \uc2 "It appears the MOF has decided that the 82-handle in USD/JPY was a step too far, and with the Kan/Ozawa leadership contest out of the way, now was the time to pounce," said \uc2 Lloyds Banking Group\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Japanese authorities need to be aggressive now and hit the market hard, fast and furious because, as time goes on, the announcement effect will dissipate, said David Bloom at \uc2 HSBC\uc2 . "The amounts become so large they start to work against international acceptance of this policy. For this to actually work, what is needed is global co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 And without this co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  there remain doubts about the long-term effectiveness of the policy.\par \par \uc2 Still, while it is impossible to say how serious the MOF is, or at what point it will ease off, said Guillaume Salomon at \uc2 TD Securities\uc2 , we can "at least say that the game has changed."\par \par \uc2 This change helped the Japanese stock market push higher, as exporters sighed with relief as the yen weakened. The Nikkei stock average closed 2.3% higher, at 9516.56, its highest closing level since Aug. 10.\par \par \uc2 And with a Japanese finance ministry official suggesting Wednesday that the authorities are prepared to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as needed to curb the yen's strength, it may be time to look at equities again.\par \par \uc2 Japanese funds continue to trade on relatively large high-teen discounts, noted Oriel Securities, and this partly reflects a lack of interest in the sector after a long period of weak returns from the Japanese stock market and funds.\par \par \uc2 However, for Japanese stock-market bulls, "we do think the discounts on the investment trusts are attractive at current levels," said Oriel.\par \par \uc2 -By Peter Nurse, Dow Jones Newswires; +44-20-7842-9288; peter.nurse@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 15, 2010 06:21 ET (10:21 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020100915e69f00247\par }\page {\par\fs20