\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG/ \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Real Time: Time For A Primer On Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 13:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Japan Real Time Report blog at blogs.wsj.com/japanrealtime.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Posted By Yoree Koh \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 The headlines took the finance world by storm Wednesday morning: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time in six years".\par \par \uc2 But what does that mean exactly? Below is a brief guide to the intricacies involved in Wednesday's yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that has traders working in overdrive.\par \par \uc2 How does yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  happen?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy with the minister, in this case Yoshihiko Noda, giving the final green light. The ministry crafts the entire strategy including the timing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and at what levels to step in. Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  involves selling yen and buying U.S. dollars, a move which fattens its foreign reserves and increases the yen supply in the market, which dilutes the value of the yen.\par \par \uc2 What prompted the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inexorable surge against the dollar has threatened the country's export-reliant economy. The toll on the shares of exporters has driven the Nikkei down considerably this year, as the rising yen made Japanese products less competitive than those of its overseas competitors. The strong yen has also added to deflationary pressures. Market concern mounted around these effects in the last two weeks, and showed itself in full form when the dollar dropped to a new 15-year low against the yen Wednesday. The MOF tends to act when it is believed the market has gained a fixed one-sided momentum, in which case the government swoops in from the other side to realign bets to ensure investors believe there's a two-way risk: In other words, it might no longer be as safe as it has been in recent months to keep buying yen.\par \par \uc2 How do you 'sterilize' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? And why would you want to leave it 'unsterilized'?\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has in a sense tossed the ball into the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's court in that it is now up to the BOJ, the institution in charge of monetary policy, to decide whether to let all the new yen slosh around in the market, or to absorb the newly-injected supply and thereby "sterilize" the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The BOJ's traditional role is to try to keep the supply and demand scales in balance and carry this out by injecting or taking money out of the market. If the BOJ chooses to let the money be, the value of the yen will likely become cheaper against the dollar, a process known as "unsterilizing" the market supply. And in this case, a cheaper yen is the objective of the MOF.\par \par \uc2 I still don't get it. Why is it a big deal?\par \par \uc2 It's a big deal because if Japan doesn't tame the strong yen, the impact on its big exporters could eventually mean reduced profits, reduced investment and ultimately threaten the country's economic recovery. That's why in a single day, Japan spent a trillion yen, or about $12 billion, in what will need to be a sustained effort if it's to be successful.\par \par \uc2 -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com }}}\uc2 . [ 15-09-10 1142GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f000z5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
