\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Noda: won't directly link policy to  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 08:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2  SHIMONOSEKI, Japan, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Bank of Japan policy board member Tadao Noda indicated on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may leave \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unsterilised but added that it would not link its policy actions directly to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday for the first time in six years, selling yen to stem a rise that is threatening a fragile economic recovery. [ID:nTOE68E02W]\par \par \uc2  "We will pursue policy responses depending on moves in the economy and in prices but the BOJ will not consider policy in a manner that links directly to the latest (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) step," Noda told a news conference in Shimonoseki, in southern Japan.\par \par \uc2  Noda, a banking industry veteran, was the sole dissenter when the BOJ cut interest rates to 0.1 percent in December 2008, arguing that pushing rates that low could distort market functions.\par \par \uc2  Noda mostly supported the adoption of unconventional steps taken during the global financial crisis, but along with one other member he opposed the BOJ's additional easing steps on March 17.  (Reporting by Rie Ishiguro; Editing by Edmund Klamann)     \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/BOJ-NODA (URGENT)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100915e69f000bq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngbli