\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Japan govt, BOJ's recent remarks on yen\b0\par\par\uc2 683 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 06:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (For more stories on the Japanese economy click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Wednesday for the first time in six years, selling yen to stem a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is threatening a fragile economic recovery. [ID:nTOE68E02W]\par \par \uc2  The dollar spiked 2 yen <JPY=> higher, off a 15-year low of 82.87 yen it had reached earlier. Two traders said the Bank of Japan, acting on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , appeared to have bought dollars at around 83 yen.\par \par \uc2  Following are recent key quotes by government and BOJ officials.\par \par \uc2  FINANCE MINISTER YOSHIHIKO NODA, Sept. 15, to reporters.\par \par \uc2  "We will take decisive steps if necessary, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while continuing to closely watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves from now on," Noda said at a news conference where he confirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  BANK OF \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  GOVERNOR MASAAKI SHIRAKAWA, Sept. 15, in a statement\par \par \uc2  "There has been growing uncertainty about the future, especially for the U.S. economy, and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets have been unstable. In these circumstances, the downside risks to Japan's economy warrant attention.\par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan strongly expects that the action taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will contribute to a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate formation.\par \par \uc2  "The Bank will, while pursuing strong monetary easing, continue to provide ample liquidity to the financial markets."\par \par \uc2  CHIEF CABINET SECRETARY YOSHITO SENGOKU, Sept. 15, to reporters\par \par \uc2  "We are making efforts to persuade, to ask for understanding from the United States and Europe.\par \par \uc2  "We cannot tell the BOJ what to due because of its independence, but I do hope that the BOJ will ease the heavy mood hanging over Japan due to the strong yen."\par \par \uc2  PRIME MINISTER NAOTO KAN, Aug. 14, quoted by Japanese media.\par \par \uc2  The sudden strengthening of the yen "has become a bit of a concern. I want to continue watching it carefully ...\par \par \uc2  "I want to be sure to communicate as necessary (with the Bank of Japan)." [ID:nTOE67D00G]\par \par \uc2  NODA, Aug. 12, to reporters.\par \par \uc2  "The government's basic stance is that excessive and disorderly moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates would have a negative impact on the stability of the economy and financial markets. We must watch them with the utmost attention. In particular I'm watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves very carefully and with great interest.\par \par \uc2  "I'm closely in touch with the prime minister and the chief cabinet secretary with regard to market moves. We will respond appropriately while carefully examining economic trends.\par \par \uc2  "Today the vice finance minister for international affairs exchanged views on market moves with a senior BOJ official, and we will keep in close contact with each other from now on.\par \par \uc2  "I'll refrain from commenting on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  "Officials (in the finance ministry) are sharing information with officials not only in the United States but other countries at the working level ... I'm not thinking about (a teleconference with other G7 members) at the moment." [ID:nTOE67B069]\par \par \uc2  SHIRAKAWA, Aug. 12, in a statement.\par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets are showing big fluctuations against the backdrop of heightened uncertainty about the U.S. economic outlook.\par \par \uc2  "The BOJ will closely watch market fluctuations and their impact on the Japanese economy." [ID:nTFD006522]\par \par \uc2  BANK OF JAPAN EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR HIROSHI NAKASO, in charge of international affairs, Aug. 12, to reporters.\par \par \uc2  "Rate checks are part of our intention to closely watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves." [ID:nTFD006523]\par \par \uc2  SHIRAKAWA, Aug. 10, news conference after board meeting.\par \par \uc2  "I acknowledge that yen rises pose a downside risk to business sentiment. We need to examine the impact on the overall economy in a balanced way.\par \par \uc2  "We spent much time debating how the recent yen rise could affect business sentiment and the Japanese economy. This is an important point for us to examine ...\par \par \uc2  "No \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in developed nations targets \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels in managing monetary policy." [ID:nTOE67809A]  (Reporting by Stanley White; Editing by Michael Watson)     \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/YEN-QUOTES (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|U|NAT|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100915e69f0007v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
