\par\par \b \uc2 NZ$ dragged down by dovish cenbank, Aussie fades\b0\par\par\uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2010\par 00:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * NZ dlr hit as RBNZ signals shallower tightening trajectory\par \par \uc2 * Aussie eases off highs vs yen as \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pauses\par \par \uc2 By Mantik Kusjanto and Wayne Cole\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY/WELLINGTON, Sept 16 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar shed more than half of a U.S. cent on Thursday while bonds surged after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scaled back its forecast of interest rates rises because of a soft economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The head of the Reserve Bank of New Zealand, Alan Bollard, added insult to injury by flatly stating the kiwi's strength was not justified by the country's fundamentals, after downgrading the bank's economic forecasts much further than expected.\par \par \uc2 "It seems to have lost faith in the recovery story, and faith, once lost, is not easily regained," said \uc2 Westpac\uc2  markets economist Michael Gordon.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi <NZD=D4> slid to $0.7237 by late afternoon, from an early $0.7320. Support now was seen at last Friday's low of $0.7228, with resistance around Wednesday's high of $0.7357.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar also faded from its highs as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the yen, prompting profit-taking on that cross.\par \par \uc2 The NZ swap curve steepened after the RBNZ kept rates at 3.0 percent as expected but sounded more dovish in its policy statement. Rates at front end of the curve fell much more than the longer end <NZDIRS> while debt <0#NZTSY=> rallied strongly.\par \par \uc2 After the rate decision, all 18 economists polled by Reuters expected rates to stay at 3.0 percent through the end of the year, compared with a 3.25 percent forecast in the previous poll. [NZ/POLL]\par \par \uc2 "We see the RBNZ remaining on hold for the rest of this year, with the first hike in March 2011," said Khoon Goh, the head of markets economics at ANZ-National.\par \par \uc2 The RBNZ said more rate rises would likely be needed over time but the tightening would be slower than previously forecast, slashing its wholesale rates forecast by about 135 bps by March 2013 from its previous forecast in June. See [ID:nSGE68E044] Markets are now pricing in 62 basis points of tightening over the next 12 months from 69 on Wednesday and compared with 79 basis points in late July. <CSRBNZ1Y=CSAU>.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, a run of upbeat Australian data has led the market to revise up sharply the chance of further rate hikes form the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  (RBA) in coming months <0#YIB;>.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the Aussie jumped to a five-month high on its New Zealand neighbour at NZ$1.2921 <AUDNZD=R>, up from NZ$1.2750 at the start of the week.\par \par \uc2 RBA Assistant Governor \uc2 Philip Lowe\uc2  reiterated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's optimistic outlook for the domestic economy, saying demand for resources from China and India could drive growth for years to come [ID:nSDYGKE6GJ].\par \par \uc2 Still the Aussie edged back to 79.70 yen <AUDJPY=R> from a four-month peak of 80.64, as the Japanese authorities surprised by not following up on Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The resulting profit-taking also nudged it down to $0.9340 <AUD=D4>, and away from the two-year peaks of $0.9457 hit earlier this week. A sharp drop in Chinese shares <.SSEC> added to the downward pressure.\par \par \uc2 Australian three-year bond futures <YTTc1> edged up 0.005 points to 95.240, while 10-year futures <YTCc1> rose 0.010 points to 94.915.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-NEWZEALAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BONDS (UPDATE1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AUF|ND|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100918e69f000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
