\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  COLUMN-Unsterilized  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 : New trick. New response?\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Weir   \par \uc2 657 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 19:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Kevin Weir is a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst for Reuters. The opinions expressed are their own.)\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen on Wednesday came as something of a surprise, but only because the authorities had chosen not to take advantage of recent market holidays in London and New York.\par \par \uc2 Many market participants had assumed, since the opportunity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in thin markets was ignored, that the "line in the sand" in the dollar-yen pair <JPY=> was somewhat lower, perhaps at 82 or even 80.\par \par \uc2 More generically, however, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's activity was hardly surprising, as the rhetoric from Japanese officialdom, and complaints from large exporters, had been prolonged and consistent.\par \par \uc2 There was, however, at least one novelty. The funds related to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain "unsterilized", meaning that the yen sold in return for dollars will not be extracted from the banking system through an issuance of bills, the Bank of Japan's normal tactic.\par \par \uc2 Wednesday's activity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market thus becomes another instrument of monetary policy and market participants will need to incorporate this new information into their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate forecasts.\par \par \uc2 The initial reaction by institutional investors to these stimuli, at least beyond the fairly obvious conclusion that selling dollars below the 83 level is unlikely to be rewarding in the near term, is that the employment of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a part of monetary policy makes it likely that the authorities will be persistent.\par \par \uc2 They will also attempt to push dollar higher against the yen rather than simply defend a given level such as 83. To the extent that a weaker yen is normally a sign of risk seeking by market participants, there was some surprise that assets such as U.S. equity futures -- which have since recovered, and moved higher -- responded sluggishly.\par \par \uc2 Some participants suggested that the timing of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a rapid response by large U.S. names unlikely, and that any changes in asset selection could be a day or two in coming.\par \par \uc2 One large fixed income manager did note that his firm is taking the opportunity to take profits in a portion of its holdings of Japanese Government Bonds (JGBs), which spiked higher in price in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For those managers with unhedged benchmarks, a weakening yen reduces the overall returns from Japanese fixed income assets, so the temptation to lighten up those holdings is strong, particularly if additional \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is anticipated.\par \par \uc2 While the general assumption is that the dollars purchased by Japan will be used to add to holdings of U.S. Treasury bills, there is some conjecture that due to the very low yields that at least some 2-year notes might be acquired.\par \par \uc2 There was also speculation, perhaps related to discussions with bank sales coverage, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself was part of a political deal to help secure PM Kan's election as head of the ruling DJP.\par \par \uc2 Managers referring to these rumors indicated that in their view it made ongoing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more likely as part of a political arrangement that is ultimately designed to help protect Japanese exporters from the consequences of an ever-stronger yen.\par \par \uc2 One London based \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales manager observed that in his experience when the Japanese authorities act, they tend to remain involved for a substantial period of time.\par \par \uc2 There still seems to be some natural uncertainty as to how aggressive the BOJ will be in trying to force the yen lower, but a consensus appears to exist that unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , by increasing the local money supply, effectively kills two birds with one stone, and is hence likely to be longer in duration and larger in scope than might otherwise be the case.\par \par \uc2 COLUMN-MARKETS/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (COLUMN)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|Z|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100915e69f0019o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
