\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-TREASURIES-Yield curve steepens on Japan buying expectations\b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 14:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers with no changes to text)\par \par \uc2 * Japanese buying of Treasuries seen in short-dated debt\par \par \uc2 * Treasury yield curve steepest in over a month\par \par \uc2 * Fed buys $3.9 billion of Treasuries on Wednesday (Adds analyst's quotes, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Chris Reese\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Sept 15 (Reuters) - Longer-dated U.S. Treasuries fell on Wednesday, steepening the Treasury yield curve as investors bet any buying by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely take place in shorter-dated debt.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, its first in six years, sparked the dollar's biggest one-day rally against the yen in nearly two years. Trader sentiment grew that the Bank of Japan will plow the resulting dollars into shorter-dated Treasuries in coming days. For details see [ID:nTOE68E02W].\par \par \uc2 "Today's move is in anticipation of that (BoJ buying)," said Anthony Valeri, market strategist with LPL Financial in San Diego, adding it was likely "short-dated issues which Japan will likely focus on."\par \par \uc2 That expected focus on shorter-dated issues hit longer-dated debt, and benchmark 10-year Treasury notes <US10YT=RR> fell 11/32 in price with the yield rising to 2.72 percent from 2.68 percent late on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 On the short end, two-year Treasury notes <US2YT=RR> rose 1/32 in price to yield 0.49 percent, down from 0.51 percent late on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The price action steepened the Treasury yield curve, with the spread between two-year yields and 10-year yields widening to 223 basis points -- marking the steepest yield curve in over a month-- from 217 basis points late on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 "People believe that the net effect (of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) would be a steepening of the yield curve," said James Caron, head of global rates research at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  in New York, adding "as the yen sells off it creates an exposure where people have to sell the back end of the U.S. rate curve -- two year yields are down because Japan is going to buy in the front end."\par \par \uc2 Traders at major \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers estimated \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday amounted to at least $20 billion. In its 2003-2004 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign, it spent about $409 billion.\par \par \uc2 Separately on Wednesday, the U.S. Federal Reserve bought $3.9 billion in U.S. government debt maturing in four to five years. It has spent $21.5 billion of funds from maturing agency bonds and mortgage-backed securities to buy Treasuries since August. For more, see [ID:nN20EDTABL]\par \par \uc2 In the cash market, five-year Treasuries <US5YT=RR> were trading little changed in price to yield 1.45 percent.\par \par \uc2 Thirty-year bonds <US30YT=RR> traded 1-6/32 lower in price to yield 3.87 percent, up from 3.80 percent late on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts were skeptical whether Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move will have a lasting impact on weakening the yen, as there has been increased market talk that the Fed will expand its balance sheet to buy Treasuries in a bid to help the U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 If U.S. growth were to slow further, analysts expect the Fed will reinstate quantitative easing measures it first adopted it late 2008 to combat the global credit crisis.\par \par \uc2 These forecasters expect the Fed could buy up to $1 trillion in Treasuries by early 2011. Such a move could push U.S. yields lower and weaken the dollar, and in turn strengthen the yen, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "This could possibly counteract the (BoJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," LPL's Valeri said.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is scheduled to hold a policy meeting next Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Thursday's U.S. data signaled slowing growth in the manufacturing sector, which has been the lone bright spot during this uneven recovery. [ID:nN15145257] ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 For a graphic on N.Y. Fed manufacturing data, see: http:/graphics.thomsonreuters.com/F/09/US_NYFED0910.gif\par \par \uc2 For a graphic on U.S. industrial output, see: http:/graphics.thomsonreuters.com/F/09/US_IPCAP0910.gif ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ (Additional reporting by Richard Leong; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BONDS (UPDATE 6, RPT)|LANGEN|DA|FN|NW|SW   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100915e69f000tg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
