\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-EU: yen  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  more effective if coordinated\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jan Strupczewski and Silke Koltrowitz   \par \uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 12:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail)\par \par \uc2 BRUSSELS/KEHRSATZ, Switzerland Sept 15 (Reuters) - The European Union gave some support on Wednesday to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the rising yen but said such action would have had more impact if had it been coordinated with others.\par \par \uc2 "Unilateral actions are not the appropriate way to deal with global imbalances," Eurogroup Chairman Jean-Claude Juncker, on a trip to Switzerland, said when asked about the Bank of Japan's action.\par \par \uc2 Japan sold yen in the market on Wednesday for the first time in six years and promised more to come in a bid to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relentless rise from hurting exporters and threatening a fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 The yen had surged to its highest against the dollar since 1995, as low U.S. interest rates have made the dollar cheap to borrow and swap for higher-yielding assets and as talk has resurfaced that the Fed might loosen policy further.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda, who will reportedly keep his post after a cabinet reshuffle, indicated Tokyo acted alone on the yen. He said he was in contact with authorities overseas.\par \par \uc2 But an EU source said Japan had not even informed the Europeans, or the United States, about the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Euro zone sources said earlier this month that there had been no discussions of European support for a potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a clear signal that coordinated help would not have been forthcoming.\par \par \uc2 The European Commission -- the bloc's executive -- echoed Juncker's line.\par \par \uc2 "We are of the opinion that coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are to be preferred, as past experience has shown that these are notably more effective than uncoordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Commission spokesman Amadeu Altafaj said in Brussels.\par \par \uc2 But he added that exchange rates out of line with fundamentals could pose problems to stability.\par \par \uc2 "Excess exchange rate volatility and exchange rates that are not in line with fundamentals may have adverse implications for economic and financial stability," Altafaj said. "Despite Japan's ongoing current account surplus, a too rapid yen appreciation could pose challenges to the recovery."\par \par \uc2 The Commission said Japan could have equally well used monetary policy instruments rather than a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Monetary policy measures are at least as likely to have an impact on the yen strength and on deflation as \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," Altafaj said.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was boosted further after an official at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not finished. It climbed about 3 percent on the day to more than 85.50 yen, having dropped to a 15-year low of 82.87 yen earlier. (Reporting by Jan Strupczewski, editing by Mike Peacock)\par \par \uc2 EU-JAPAN/YEN (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABX|BNX|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100915e69f000nv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
