\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens Against Dollar After  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Govt  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 17:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--The Brazilian real reversed course on Wednesday, weakening against the U.S. dollar after the Japanese government rattled global markets earlier in the day as it sought to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 "The Japanese move has given pause to everyone in the market here in Brazil," said a Sao Paulo-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. "The strength of the U.S. dollar against the yen and the euro Wednesday has helped prevent a strengthening of the real beyond the BRL1.70 barrier."\par \par \uc2 Japan sold yen in the market on Wednesday for the first time in six years and promised more to come in a bid to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's relentless rise from hurting exporters and threatening a fragile economic recovery.\par \par \uc2 At 1530 GMT, the real was trading at BRL1.7233 per dollar, weaker against Tuesday's close of BRL1.7055.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real gained against the dollar for six straight sessions through Tuesday, but stalled just as it was approaching the key BRL1.70 test. The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added a further note of caution to the market on Wednesday, as it held an auction to buy dollars at BRL1.713.\par \par \uc2 "The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been making a determined effort to hold the line at BRL1.70," said Paulo Fujisaki, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Sao Paulo's Socopa brokerage. "But there is no guarantee the BRL1.70 line will hold forever."\par \par \uc2 Since early September, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been purchasing dollars at twice-daily snap auctions in order to avoid a sharp rise in the real. Previously, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tended to hold only a single daily auction.\par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was interested in holding the line against a sharp appreciation of the real since a strong real hurts exports.\par \par \uc2 Socopa's Fujisaki said the real has been gaining strength in recent days because of heavy inflows of dollars from overseas bond placements. Meanwhile, investors have been bringing in dollars ahead of a massive offer of shares later this month by state-controlled oil company \uc2 Petrobras\uc2  (PBR, PETR4.BR).\par \par \uc2 -By Tom Murphy, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3544-7090; brazil@dowjones.com [ 15-09-10 1552GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f0018w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
