\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 690 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 16:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par US INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT RISES 0.2% IN AUGUST \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. industrial production rises a second straight month, suggesting the sector that once was the primary driver of growth hasn't completely tapered off. Capacity utilization rises to 74.7%. Economists expected output to rise 0.3% with a factory operating rate of 75%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US IMPORT PRICES RISE 0.6% IN AUGUST \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. import prices rise more than expected amid higher energy and food prices, a move that should help quell fears that the economy may fall into deflation. Economists were expecting a more modest 0.3% rise in August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NY MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY EXPANDS AT SLOWER PACE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York manufacturing activity expands this month but at a slower pace than in August, according to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Empire State Manufacturing Survey, while hiring continues to rebound.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US MORTGAGE-REFINANCE ACTIVITY SLUMPS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The volume of mortgage applications filed in the U.S. last week drops 8.9% from the previous week, the Mortgage Bankers Association reports, on declines in refinancing activity.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCKS OPEN LOWER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US stocks open lower as investors risk appetites are pressured by gains in the dollar following Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to try to stem the yen's rise. Also, U.S. import prices improve but New York manufacturing activity slows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREENSPAN SAYS STIMULUS FELL SHORT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Fed chairman says that government needs to get out of the way and let businesses take over the recovery, and that at this point, "we'd probably be better off doing less than more" to stimulate the economy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HEALTH OF FANNIE, FREDDIE CRUCIAL TO MORTGAGE MARKET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Fannie Mae\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Freddie Mac\f28 \uc2 \f2  will have to make an orderly withdrawal from markets or mortgage rates would skyrocket and most homeowners would be unable to obtain mortgage credit, says one Treasury official.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LAUNCHES Y1T \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , YEN TUMBLES \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for the first time in more than six years, launching a wave of yen selling totaling an estimated Y1 trillion to counter what it calls "the severe economic conditions' facing the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE INFLATION SLIPS FURTHER BELOW ECB TARGET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's annual inflation rate dips in line with expectations in August, indicating the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has room to maintain its ultra-loose monetary policy, data from the EU's Eurostat statistics agency shows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHEVRON NEAR NATURAL GAS DEAL WITH CNPC \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chevron\f28 \uc2 \f2  is close to an initial deal with \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to import natural gas from Australia, in the energy industry's latest bet that growing demand from China will justify projects aimed at tapping new gas supplies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Beat Watch \par A TURNING POINT FOR THE LABOR MOVEMENT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the U.K.'s Trades Union Congress meets in Manchester vowing to fight the expected job cuts in the upcoming spending review, it could find the struggle has just got a little harder as employment may have reached a turning point.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Focus \par SWEDEN'S REINFELDT IN ECONOMIC BOOST AS VOTE NEARS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swedish Prime Minister Fredrik Reinfeldt heads into Sunday's general election on the crest of the sharpest economic recovery among Europe's major countries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Money Talks \par TURNING JAPANESE? I REALLY DON'T THINK SO.... \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ever since the financial crisis struck, a significant group of Keynesian economists has warned that the U.S. and other leading economies run the risk of turning Japanese.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCKS OPEN LOWER AS JAPANESE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  BOOSTS DOLLAR \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US stocks open lower as Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  boosts the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURYS FALL AFTER \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO CURB YEN'S GAINS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Longer-dated Treasurys fall after Japan moves to curb the yen's gains.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YEN CONTINUES FALL; INVESTORS ON WATCH FOR JAPAN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar gains further ground against the yen after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE WEAKER NEAR $75/BBL AHEAD OF US OIL DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude trades lower ahead of key U.S. DOE data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GOLD FLAT AS TRADERS CASH IN ON RECORD HIGHS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Gold futures are flat as traders sell holding to cash in on record highs. [ 15-09-10 1401GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f0014u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
