\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 710 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 15:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOP STORIES \par  \par US IMPORT PRICES RISE 0.6% IN AUGUST \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. import prices rise more than expected amid higher energy and food prices, a move that should help quell fears that the economy may fall into deflation. Economists were expecting a more modest 0.3% rise in August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NY MANUFACTURING ACTIVITY EXPANDS AT SLOWER PACE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New York manufacturing activity expands this month but at a slower pace than in August, according to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Empire State Manufacturing Survey, while hiring continues to rebound.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US MORTGAGE-REFINANCE ACTIVITY SLUMPS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The volume of mortgage applications filed in the U.S. last week drops 8.9% from the previous week, the Mortgage Bankers Association reports, on declines in refinancing activity.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SPLASHES Y1 TRILLION TO COOL YEN \par  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market for the first time in more than six years, launching a wave of yen selling totaling an estimated Y1 trillion to counter what it calls "the severe economic conditions' facing the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EURO-ZONE INFLATION SLIPS FURTHER BELOW ECB TARGET \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro zone's annual inflation rate dips in line with expectations in August, indicating the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has room to maintain its ultra-loose monetary policy, data from the EU's Eurostat statistics agency shows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES DROP AS NY FED DATA WEAKENS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US stock futures move lower after import prices show a 0.6% rise in August from July, and New York manufacturing activity shows expansion in September, but at a slower pace than in August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHEVRON NEAR NATURAL GAS DEAL WITH CNPC \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chevron\f28 \uc2 \f2  is close to an initial deal with \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to import natural gas from Australia, in the energy industry's latest bet that growing demand from China will justify projects aimed at tapping new gas supplies.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par IRAQ GAS AUCTION STILL OCT 1, DELAY POSSIBLE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Iraq is still planning to hold a licensing auction to award three major gas field licenses on its scheduled time Oct. 1 after 11 international companies paid the participating fees, but an Iraqi oil official concedes that a delay is possible.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURY TO SELL LINCOLN NATIONAL WARRANTS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury plans to auction the 13 million warrant positions the government acquired from Lincoln National, completely freeing the company from the government's Troubled Asset Relief Program.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par STRENGTHENING IGOR HEADS TOWARD BERMUDA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Category-four Hurricane Igor, the strongest Atlantic storm of 2010, barrels toward Bermuda after whipping up much of the Caribbean. Igor threatens to dump more rain on Mexico, already struggling with flooding.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par Video \par JAPAN SELLS YEN FOR FIRST TIME IN 6 YEARS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To help its ailing economy and lift the stock market, Japan sells its own \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sending the dollar to a 15-year low. Dow Jones Newswires' Mark Cranfield reports. -- Watch video.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Focus \par SWEDEN'S REINFELDT IN ECONOMIC BOOST AS VOTE NEARS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Swedish Prime Minister Fredrik Reinfeldt heads into Sunday's general election on the crest of the sharpest economic recovery among Europe's major countries.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Money Talks \par TURNING JAPANESE? I REALLY DON'T THINK SO.... \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ever since the financial crisis struck, a significant group of Keynesian economists has warned that the U.S. and other leading economies run the risk of turning Japanese.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Heard on the Street \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NEEDS TO BE BIG IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Is Tokyo going to take a firehose to a fight with a tsunami, asks James Simms, after the Japanese government ended a six-year moratorium on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, selling the yen in an effort to reverse its recent rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ============ MARKETS ACTION ============ \par  \par US STOCK FUTURES MOVE LOWER AS NY FED DATA WEAKENS; DJIA OFF 49 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 US stock futures slip after weak NY Fed manufacturing data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TREASURYS FALL AFTER YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasurys drop investors book profits in wake of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par YEN CONTINUES FALL; INVESTORS ON WATCH FOR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar gains further ground against the yen after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan forex intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CRUDE LOWER AS PRESSURE BUILDS AHEAD OF DOE DATA \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude trades lower ahead of key U.S. DOE data.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SPOT GOLD PAUSES, RALLY TO $1,300/OZ SEEN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spot gold consolidates gains after rallying to new record highs. [ 15-09-10 1309GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f0012w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
