\par\par \b \uc2 WSJ BLOG/ \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  Real Time: Shirakawa And Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 251 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 13:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (This story has been posted on The Wall Street Journal Online's Japan Real Time Report blog at blogs.wsj.com/japanrealtime.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    Posted By Yuka Hayashi and Jacob Schlesinger \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 After the finance ministry made the dramatic announcement Wednesday that it had formally begun yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa issued a robust statement of confidence: "The Bank of Japan strongly expects that the action taken by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will contribute to a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate formation."\par \par \uc2 Analysts and economists are more skeptical. Japanese officials said they were acting on their own. And the experts tend to think government \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rarely effective--and then, only if it's done in coordination with other countries.\par \par \uc2 Take, for example, this quote from a respected Kyoto University economist in a 2008 book, "Modern Monetary Policy in Theory and Practice":\par \par \uc2 "When the countries concerned make a coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on a unified judgment about the level of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, there are cases in which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is effective. In other words, it's hard in general to expect a market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without those conditions to be effective."\par \par \uc2 And in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's case, those conditions are conspicuous by their absence.\par \par \uc2 The author's name? Masaaki Shirakawa. He became governor of the Bank of Japan in April 2008.\par \par \uc2 -For continuously updated news from The Wall Street Journal, see WSJ.com at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://wsj.com}}}\uc2 . [ 15-09-10 1135GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f000yr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
