\par\par \b \uc2 Euro Holds Firm As Yen  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Impact Limited\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Martin   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 11:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--Fears of a collapse in the euro against the dollar in the event of a dollar-buying splurge by the Bank of Japan have proven unfounded, as the broader impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's super-sized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight appears so far limited.\par \par \uc2 Many analysts have pondered over recent weeks whether the long-speculated move by Japanese authorities to weaken the sky-high yen could be the trigger for a widespread run higher in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , toppling the rally in the euro that has persisted since June. Some still believe that the sting increases the chances of Switzerland re-entering the market to weaken the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 In the event, though, the 3% jump in the dollar against the yen Wednesday--a huge intraday move--has left the euro and most other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  little changed, and market-watchers generally expect the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain limited to the yen for now.\par \par \uc2 "It's too early to think that this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by one Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be enough to influence the euro against the dollar," said Paul Robson, a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at the Royal Bank of Scotland PLC in London.\par \par \uc2 At 0920 GMT Wednesday, the dollar was trading at Y85.42 against the yen, according to trading system EBS. The euro was at $1.2978, while the pound was at $1.5517.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at CHF1.3036 against the Swiss franc, leaving it a substantial 0.8% above its lowest point of the day. Similarly, the dollar was at CHF1.0044, marking a 1% climb from significantly below parity in earlier trading.\par \par \uc2 -By Katie Martin, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9346; katie.martin@dowjones.com [ 15-09-10 0954GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f000tp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
