\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,407 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 11:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LAUNCHES \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , YEN DOWN SHARPLY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday for the first time in more than six years, launching a wave of yen selling to deal with "severe economic conditions" facing the country. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ NODA: TO PROVIDE AMPLE FUNDS, MAKING USE OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FUNDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will make use of yen sold in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , policy board member Tadao Noda said Wednesday, indicating that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not soak up the extra \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the market. (published 0673 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ NODA VOWS 'SWIFT AND DECISIVE' ACTION IF NECESSARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Bank of Japan policy board member said Wednesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will take policy steps "swiftly and decisively" if the country's economic recovery falters and its deflationary trend worsens. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US FED HAS NO IMMEDIATE COMMENT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. Federal Reserve late Tuesday said it had no immediate comment on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to weaken the yen. (published 0334 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF OFFICIAL: USUALLY, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  INVOLVES REPEATED ACTION \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market usually involved repeated action, not one-off moves, a Japanese finance ministry official said Wednesday, suggesting the authorities are prepared to continue \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as needed to curb the yen's strength. (published 0426 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN GOVT SENGOKU: FINANCE MINISTER LIKELY SAW Y82 LEVEL AS RED LINE -NIKKEI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda likely considered the dollar's fall below Y83.00 to have been a breach of a critical threshold warranting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the government's top spokesman suggested Wednesday after Tokyo waded into markets to curb the yen's strength, the Nikkei reported. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GERMAN MERKEL: GERMANY IS NOW EUROPE'S GROWTH ENGINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German Chancellor Angela Merkel Wednesday painted a rosy picture of the economy, pointing to higher growth and lower unemployment. (published 0816 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOE'S MILES: UK INFLATION LIKELY ABOVE 3% FOR MONTHS - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K.'s inflation rate is likely to stay above 3% "for a few good months yet", but will probably fall back towards the Bank of England's target during 2011, BOE Monetary Policy Committee member David Miles was quoted as saying Wednesday. (published 0821 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK AUG CLAIMANT JOBLESS RISES UNEXPECTEDLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. claimant count unemployment rose in August for the first time since January this year, hinting at tough times ahead once government spending cuts begin to bite in earnest, data showed Wednesday. (published 0839 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA PBOC ADVISER: DON'T SEE CONDITIONS FOR BIG RISE IN YUAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China adviser Li Daokui said Wednesday he doesn't see conditions for a large appreciation for the yuan because China's trade surplus is already shrinking. (published 0745 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: MONETARY POLICY MUST RETURN TO NORMAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's monetary policy must return to normal, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said Wednesday, adding the rapid increase in lending last year created some asset price problems. (published 0454 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UK BUSINESS SECRETARY CABLE: EMERGING MARKETS OPPORTUNITY NOT THREAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. coalition government sees key emerging markets as an economic "opportunity" and welcomes investment from overseas, including sovereign wealth funds, Business Secretary Vince Cable said Wednesday. (published 0839 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA FDI GROWTH DROPS AGAIN, BUT TREND UNCLEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Growth in foreign direct investment in China slowed sharply for the second consecutive month in August, data issued Wednesday showed, but some economists said a statistical quirk played a big role and monthly fluctuations don't reflect the overall trend. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PBOC ADVISER: PROPERTY MARKET ADJUSTMENTS TO TAKE 2-3 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It will take two to three years for China's property market to complete the adjustments induced by the tightening measures introduced earlier this year to curb speculation and lower prices, People's Bank of China adviser Xia Bin said Wednesday. (published 0524 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA STATISTICS BUREAU CHIEF: CHINA INFLATION 'RELATIVELY STABLE' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's inflation is "relatively stable," Ma Jiantang, head of the National Bureau of Statistics, said Wednesday. (published 0439 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (published 0516 GMT) \par  \par SCHWARZENEGGER URGES CONGRESS TO RATIFY TRADE PACTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 California Gov. Arnold Schwarzenegger urged the U.S. Congress Wednesday to ratify stalled free trade agreements including one with South Korea if it wants to start "putting people back to work." (published 0849 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA: GROUNDLESS TO SAY CHINA MANIPULATING YUAN TO BOOST TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is groundless to say China manipulates its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost foreign trade, Commerce Ministry spokesman Yao Jian said Wednesday at a news conference. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCE MINISTER: TURKISH ECONOMY MAY GROW 6%-7% IN 2010 - IHA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Turkish Finance Minister Mehmet Simsek said Wednesday that the Turkish economy is likely to grow between 6% and 7% this year, the Ihlas News Agency, or IHA, reported. (published 0734 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSSIE CONSUMER SENTIMENT, HOUSING DISAPPOINT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Even as Australian consumer confidence dipped broadly in September, economists and markets aren't backpedaling from their view that the local economy is still booming and the central will get back to hiking interest rates. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SINGAPORE 2Q UNEMPLOYMENT FLAT AT 2.2% SEASONALLY ADJ VS 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's unemployment rate was unchanged at 2.2% in the second quarter from the first, according to the Ministry of Manpower's final estimates released Wednesday. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par MONEY TALKS: FOREIGN INVESTORS NOT RUSHING BACK TO THAILAND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A pick up in foreign direct investment in Thailand after a period of political troubles in Bangkok is not the start of a trend. (published 0750 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: SWISS FRANC'S UPSIDE IS LIMITED NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Calling time on the Swiss franc rally. At the moment, there is still plenty of reason for bulls to continue buying the Swiss \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The Swiss economy continues to outperform its neighbors and uncertainty over the global recovery makes the franc attractive as a safe haven. (published 0716 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHARTING ASIA: STERLING MAY RISE TO NZ$2.1464 IN COMING DAYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Higher-than-expected U.K. consumer price inflation data as well as broad-based U.S. dollar weakness have conspired to help sterling to rally one percent from its recent seven-week lows against the Kiwi dollar. Technical charts suggest sterling, quoted at NZ$2.1139 at 0550 GMT Wednesday, could advance to NZ$2.1464, and possibly to NZ$2.1520, in coming days. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BONDS LOOK TO EXTEND GAINS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: The recovery off Monday's bull hammer low at 129.53 is running into resistance between 130.89 and 131.10. However, there is room for projected resistance at 131.43, which provides the limit for corrective upside scope. A break above 131.43 would leave 129.53 as a bear failure low, and open the Sep. 8 lower high at 132.14. The 130.00 level has become short-term pivotal support, which is protected by 130.27. Weekly chart BUND trend: Bearish. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: JPY WEAKNESS UNSUSTAINABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Tuesday's high at 1.3034 is likely to face renewed bull pressure as the 1.3000 level is breached to the upside for the first time since Aug. 11. Resistance at 1.3075 will be the initial target, but scope has been created for further gains towards the 1.3155/80 resistance cluster this week. Support lies at 1.2940, but downside risk looks limited to the 1.2895 area. Weekly chart EUR/USD trend: Bullish. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MONEY TALKS: JAPAN TAKES ON THE $4 TRILLION MONSTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Those working on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  desk at the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may find themselves selling lots and lots of yen in the next 24 hours. (published 0507 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: HK JUNE-AUGUST JOBLESS LIKELY UNCHANGED AT 4.3% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's unemployment rate likely held steady in the three months ended Aug. 31, but economists said it could fall toward the end of the year as the city's economy continues to grow. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: RBI MAY LIFT INDIA RATES 25BPS AS INFLATION WEIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to raise its two key policy rates by 25 basis points each Thursday as it seeks to restrain inflationary expectations even as the economy continues growing strongly. (published 0617 GMT) [ 15-09-10 0901GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f000qt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
