\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Asian Summary\b0\par\par\uc2 445 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 08:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0627 GMT [Dow Jones]\par \par \uc2 Regional markets mixed; Nikkei sharply up on JPY selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities; Nikkei Stock Average +2.3% at 9516.56 vs intraday low of 9199.08. S&P/ASX 200 +0.7%, Kospi +0.5%, Shanghai Composite off 0.6%, HSI +0.1%, Taiex +0.4%, STI +0.5%, KLCI down 0.3%, SET down 1.3%, NZX-50 off 0.1%; Indonesia +3.8% in catch-up after holidays there.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets roiled by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for first time in over 6 years with wave of JPY selling to deal with "severe economic conditions" facing country. USD/JPY at 84.88 (earlier hit 85.08) vs 83.08 late NY Tuesday, off new 15-year low of 82.87 before \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . EUR/USD at 1.2991 vs 1.3020 in late NY trade Tuesday, EUR/JPY at 110.26 vs 108.20. Regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also weaken in tandem with JPY; players fear Asian central banks' could follow \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lead. "We conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier to curb excessive fluctuations in exchange rates. We will continue to closely monitor movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will take decisive steps, including \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , when necessary," \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda says in news conference. \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if USD/SGD falls below 1.3300, says person familiar \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's thinking; USD/SGD last at 1.3366.\par \par \uc2 Mixed Australia data: index of consumer sentiment fell 5% on-month in September to 113.2 points seasonally adjusted vs 119.2 August, say \uc2 Westpac Banking Corp\uc2 ., Melbourne Institute; 2Q total house, apartment starts +0.8% on-quarter to seasonally adjusted 44,899; worse than +3.0% forecast. But index of job vacancies for skilled workers +0.1% on-month in September, 16% higher so far on the year. South Korea August jobless rate at 3.4% seasonally adjusted, down from 3.7% in July; country's August exports +27.7% on-year revised at $36.97 billion, imports +28.6% on-year revised at $35.25 billion, trade surplus revised to $1.72 billion vs $2.08 billion. China August FDI at $7.6 billion, +1.38% on-year; compares with $6.92 billion in July, +29.2% on-year, rapid deceleration from June's +39.6%. Singapore unemployment rate unchanged at 2.2% in 2Q vs 1Q.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold at $1,268.70 per troy ounce, flat vs New York Tuesday. October crude oil futures down 55 cents at $76.25/bbl. [ 15-09-10 0637GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f000ga\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
