\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Yen Plunges Vs Rivals After  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Andrew Monahan   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 935 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 08:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The yen plunged against its rivals Wednesday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted its first \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in six and a half years.\par \par \uc2 The move by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's authority for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , pushed the yen down sharply against the dollar, euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said Japanese authorities repeatedly bought the dollar against the yen, starting in morning trade in Tokyo around 0130 GMT. That sent the greenback to a high of Y85.14 in the afternoon, up from the fresh 15-year low at Y82.87 the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had marked in the morning shortly before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  began.\par \par \uc2 Local traders estimated the yen sales at around Y200 billion to Y300 billion ($2.4 billion to $3.6 billion) in the first few minutes alone, and said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued even after the dollar climbed above Y85.\par \par \uc2 But dealers questioned whether even sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could help the dollar against the yen, as the greenback remains plagued by broader problems, chief among them expectations that weak U.S. economic data could prompt the U.S. Federal Reserve to take further easing action ahead. While Tokyo's decision to step into markets after the dollar fell below Y83.00 will likely keep the U.S. unit above that level in the near term, many dealers are skeptical that Japan will be able to keep the dollar above Y85.00, a level they say the government is likely targeting.\par \par \uc2 "I'd give the yen about a 60% chance of staying strong," said Hideki Amikura, deputy general manager at Nomura Trust and Banking. Any signals on further easing from the Fed's Open Market Committee, which meets next week, could frustrate the Japanese government's attempts to push up the dollar-yen rate, Amikura said. For those reasons, the dollar is likely to trade in a Y83.00-Y85.00 band in the coming weeks, as Japanese exporters and other market participants sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on any further rises, he said.\par \par \uc2 At 0550 GMT, the dollar stood at Y84.95, up from Y83.08 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was also sharply higher against the yen, at Y110.32 from Y108.20. The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was lower against the dollar, at $1.2989 compared with $1.3020. The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the yen and euro, was up at 81.542 from 81.074.\par \par \uc2 News of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sent the dollar higher against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in particular the euro and the British pound. Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the Korean won, Taiwan dollar, Singapore dollar and Chinese yuan also fell quickly, as analysts say that central banks in the region, which \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  often in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, now may have a stronger argument to weaken their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and boost the competitiveness of their own export sectors.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa said Wednesday he hopes the government's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stabilize the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, following the recent yen rally. He also said that the BOJ will continue to maintain "strong monetary easing."\par \par \uc2 But Shirakawa didn't say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will sterilize the funds released for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- a key point since an unsterilized \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would increase \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary base, potentially creating some inflation in the deflation-stricken country. The Nikkei reported that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had decided Wednesday not to absorb the funds that flew into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market through the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , citing sources familiar with the matter.\par \par \uc2 Observers expressed skepticism that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will result in a weaker yen against the dollar on a sustained basis, given the dollar's strong downtrend in recent months, as U.S. rates fell on expectations that the Fed will keep an ultra-easy monetary policy in place at least until late 2011 or 2012.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't stop the trend and certainly can't reverse it," said Richard Yetsenga, a Hong Kong-based \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 HSBC\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japan's Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a unilateral move. U.S. Treasury officials declined to comment immediately, but any later reaction from Washington will be watched with interest, given the general U.S. stance against \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 01:50 EST / 0550 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High    Low      12/31 \par  \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              84.89-90   83.08-11   +2.18  85.13   82.88    -8.80 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.2991-93  1.2995-98  -0.03  1.3022  1.2956   -9.26 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.5496-01  1.5548-54  -0.33  1.5555  1.5472   -4.13 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.0003-05  0.9955-65  +0.48  1.0038  0.9950   -3.39 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.0303-05  1.0270-72  +0.32  1.0319  1.0256   -2.00 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.9376-81  0.9405-10  -0.31  0.9428  0.9358   +4.37 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7325-35  0.7338-48  -0.18  0.7352  0.7309   +0.95 \par Euro Rates \par EUR/JPY Yen              110.28-30  107.97-02  +2.14  110.42  107.75  -17.24 \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Andrew Monahan, Dow Jones Newswires; 81-3-6269-2783; andrew.monahan@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (David Roman, Takashi Mochizuki and Takashi Nakamichi contributed to this article.) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 15-09-10 0630GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1034 1863 28038 4162   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f000fm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
