\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 815 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 05:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET; CITES INSTABILITY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday for the first time since 2004, saying it acted in the face of "severe economic conditions" facing the country. (published 0253 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ NODA: MUST TAKE NECESSARY STEPS SWIFTLY, DECISIVELY IF NEEDED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Bank of Japan policy board member said Wednesday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will take necessary policy steps "swiftly and decisively" if the country's economy shows clear signs of worsening and if deflation threatens to drag. (published 0233 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US TREASURY DECLINES TO COMMENT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  YEN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury officials declined to comment late Tuesday on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ NISHIMURA: TO HELP STRENGTHEN FINANCIAL INFRASTRUCTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura said Wednesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will keep supporting initiatives to strengthen the nation's financial market infrastructure. (published 0103 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA AUGUST FDI UP 1.38% ON YEAR AT $7.6 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China attracted $7.6 billion worth of foreign direct investment in August, up 1.38% from a year earlier, the Ministry of Commerce said Wednesday. (published 0211 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA YUAN HITS FRESH HIGH WEDNESDAY ON WEAK DOLLAR, FIXING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan hit another high against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  guided the dollar/yuan exchange rate to a new low for the fourth consecutive trading session following the dollar's slump overnight and ahead of key U.S. Congressional hearings on Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA: GROUNDLESS TO SAY CHINA MANIPULATING YUAN TO BOOST TRADE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It is groundless to say China manipulates its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost foreign trade, Commerce Ministry spokesman Yao Jian said Wednesday at a news conference. (published 0256 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: S KOREA JOBLESS RATE FALLS IN SIGN OF GROWING OPTIMISM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's unemployment rate fell significantly in August as the private sector stepped up hiring to meet growing demand from both domestic and external markets. (published 0246 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN CONSUMER SENTIMENT INDEX DOWN 5.0% IN SEPTEMBER VS AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of consumer sentiment in Australia fell 5% in September from August. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN HOUSING STARTS +0.8% IN 2Q VS 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The total number of houses and apartments that started construction in Australia in the second quarter of 2010 rose 0.8% to a seasonally adjusted 44,899 from the first quarter. (published 0132 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN SKILLED VACANCIES INDEX +0.1% IN SEP VS AUG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of job vacancies for skilled workers in Australia rose by 0.1% in September from August, and was 16% higher on year, the Department of Employment said Wednesday. (published 0115 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE 2Q UNEMPLOYMENT FLAT AT 2.2% SEASONALLY ADJ VS 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's unemployment rate was unchanged at 2.2% in the second quarter from the first, according to the Ministry of Manpower's final estimates released Wednesday. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: PHILIPPINES JOBLESS RATE EASES TO 6.9% IN JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The unemployment rate in the Philippines eased in July from a two-year high in April as the economy added around 930,000 jobs, mostly in agriculture, the latest jobs survey of the National Statistics Office showed Wednesday. (published 0208 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ: SOUTH KOREA'S REAL-ESTATE SLUMP COULD CHOKE ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea recovered quickly from the global economic downturn that began two years ago, spurred by a cheap \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that boosted exports, but the country now is experiencing a slump in real estate that economists said could restrain growth. (published 2044 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par LOOMING DEBT BURDEN GETTING REPAID, KICKED DOWN THE ROAD -MOODY'S \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Companies are making progress paying down a looming block of debt due to mature in the next few years, but much of it has simply been pushed a bit further down the road, according to a new report. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WOOLWORTHS PRICES US$1.25B OF SENIOR NOTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Woolworths Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has priced a US$1.25 billion bond issue, some of which will be used to pay off a share market buyback. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA FINANCE LIKELY TO PRICE BENCHMARK DOLLAR BOND WED - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned policy financing arm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Finance Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to sell a benchmark six-year dollar-denominated bond that is expected to price sometime Wednesday, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires. (published 0220 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =POINT OF VIEW: FED'S BULLARD ON JOBLESSNESS: AT LEAST SOME IS STRUCTURAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Here's another view on a key question for the U.S.: how much of the stubbornly high unemployment rate represents structural issues rather than simply an economy bumping along at a too-low growth rate to absorb new entrants and make a dent in those already out of work. (published 1928 GMT) [ 15-09-10 0301GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f00077\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
