\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 645 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 04:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER CONFIRMS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister confirmed that the authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Wednesday as the dollar fell below the key level of Y83. (published 0158 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ NISHIMURA: TO HELP STRENGTHEN FINANCIAL INFRASTRUCTURE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Deputy Gov. Kiyohiko Nishimura said Wednesday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will keep supporting initiatives to strengthen the nation's financial market infrastructure. (published 0103 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN CONSUMER SENTIMENT INDEX DOWN 5.0% IN SEPTEMBER VS AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of consumer sentiment in Australia fell 5% in September from August. (published 0030 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN HOUSING STARTS +0.8% IN 2Q VS 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The total number of houses and apartments that started construction in Australia in the second quarter of 2010 rose 0.8% to a seasonally adjusted 44,899 from the first quarter. (published 0132 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN SKILLED VACANCIES INDEX +0.1% IN SEP VS AUG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An index of job vacancies for skilled workers in Australia rose by 0.1% in September from August, and was 16% higher on year, the Department of Employment said Wednesday. (published 0115 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA AUG SEASONALLY ADJUSTED JOBLESS RATE FALLS TO 3.4% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's unemployment rate fell significantly in August from a month earlier, reversing two months of rise, as the private sector, particularly manufacturers, continued to hire more to meet growing demand from home and overseas. (published 2321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SINGAPORE 2Q UNEMPLOYMENT FLAT AT 2.2% SEASONALLY ADJ VS 1Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's unemployment rate was unchanged at 2.2% in the second quarter from the first, according to the Ministry of Manpower's final estimates released Wednesday. (published 0149 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par WOOLWORTHS PRICES US$1.25B OF SENIOR NOTES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Woolworths Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it has priced a US$1.25 billion bond issue, some of which will be used to pay off a share market buyback. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ: SOUTH KOREA'S REAL-ESTATE SLUMP COULD CHOKE ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea recovered quickly from the global economic downturn that began two years ago, spurred by a cheap \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that boosted exports, but the country now is experiencing a slump in real estate that economists said could restrain growth. (published 2044 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ: RICHMOND FED'S LACKER WANTS HIGH THRESHOLD FOR MORE FED ACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Jeffrey Lacker, president of the Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond, sees modest growth in 2011, little change in inflation and little to spur the Fed to take new actions to support the economy. (published 2201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ: FED WRESTLES OVER NEXT STEPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve officials will wrestle with a vexing question at their Sept. 21 meeting: How weak does the economy have to get, and for how long, to warrant taking new steps to boost growth? (published 2100 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par LOOMING DEBT BURDEN GETTING REPAID, KICKED DOWN THE ROAD -MOODY'S \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Companies are making progress paying down a looming block of debt due to mature in the next few years, but much of it has simply been pushed a bit further down the road, according to a new report. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =NY FED MARKET GROUP OFFERS FINAL GUIDELINES FOR BOND TRADING ACTIVITIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An industry group associated with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York\f28 \uc2 \f2  released Tuesday a final report detailing what it considers to be "best practices" for trading across a wide range of fixed-income securities. (published 1953 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =POINT OF VIEW: FED'S BULLARD ON JOBLESSNESS: AT LEAST SOME IS STRUCTURAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Here's another view on a key question for the U.S.: how much of the stubbornly high unemployment rate represents structural issues rather than simply an economy bumping along at a too-low growth rate to absorb new entrants and make a dent in those already out of work. (published 1928 GMT) [ 15-09-10 0200GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100915e69f0004p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
